[34m##[0m[37m [0m[34mRoot cause[0m

[37mYour[0m[37m [0m[32m`[0m[32mpip[0m[32m`[0m[37m [0m[1;33m**[0m[1;33mlauncher scripts existed but the actual [0m[1;32m`[0m[1;32mpip[0m[1;32m`[0m[1;33m package was deleted.[0m[1;33m**[0m

[32m`[0m[32m/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/[0m[32m`[0m[37m contained only leftovers[0m[37m:[0m

[37m```[0m
[37mREADME[0m[37m.txt[0m
[37mpip-[0m[37m24.3.1.d[0m[37mist-info/     ← metadata[0m[37m survived[0m
[37m```[0m

[37mThe [0m[32m`[0m[32mpip/[0m[32m`[0m[37m directory itself was[0m[37m gone ([0m[37msite-packages was[0m[37m last[0m[37m modified Oct 31 13[0m[37m:45,[0m[37m while the metadata[0m[37m dated[0m[37m back[0m[37m to the[0m[37m image build). So every [0m[32m`[0m[32mpip[0m[32m`[0m[37m invocation died[0m[37m at import time[0m[37m:[0m

[37m```[0m
[37m$[0m[37m pip[0m[37m3 --version[0m
[37mTrace[0m[37mback (most recent call last[0m[37m):[0m
[37m  File "/usr/local[0m[37m/bin/pip3", line[0m[37m 5, in <module[0m[38;5;9m>[0m
[38;5;9m    from pip.[0m[35m_[0m[35minternal.cli.main import main[0m
[35mModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'[0m
[35m```[0m

[35mThis is a classic half-deleted install: something removed the package tree but left `dist-info` behind. That leftover metadata is also why the obvious fix fails — `ensurepip` checks the metadata first:[0m

[35m```[0m
[35m$ python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip[0m
[35mRequirement already satisfied: pip in .../site-packages (24.3.1)   ← lies[0m
[35m```[0m

[35m## The fix[0m

[35m1. Moved the orphaned metadata out of the way (backed up to `/tmp/pip-24.3.1.dist-info.bak`):[0m
[35m   ```bash[0m
[35m   mv /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info /tmp/pip-24.3.1.dist-info.bak[0m
